# python practice 

just learning python rn and trying to understand how stuff actually works instead of js memorizing things.

## what ive learnt so far

- variables — storing values and using them later
- input and print** — taking input from the user and displaying stuff
- if, elif and else — making decisions based on conditions
- dictionaries — storing data using keys and values
- lists — keeping multiple values in one place
- sets — storing unique values without duplicates
- checking values — seeing if a username exists in a dictionary
- nested dictionaries — storing more information inside a user account
- basic authentication logic — making a simple signup system that stores usernames and passwords, then checking login details

## what im working on

currently trying to make a basic account system using python.

the idea is pretty simple:
- enter a username and password
- create an account if the username doesnt already exist
- stop duplicate usernames
- check login details
- show if the login was successful or not

## whats next

- loops
- functions
- making the program run through a menu
- saving user data so it doesnt disappear when the program closes
- making some small projects to actually practice everything

still learning so the code is probably not the cleanest rn but thats kinda the point lol. gotta start somewhere 💀

